target/
fixtures
# ...but the per-crate PINS are tracked on purpose: 48 files under
# crates/ec-av1/fixtures/*.obu are committed fixtures (captured streams with a
# recorded sha256/recipe in their gate's doc comment) and they must travel
# with the repo. A bare `fixtures` rule ignores them at EVERY depth, so they
# are only in history because someone used `git add -f` -- and a new pin then
# fails a plain `git add` with a hint that reads like noise. Measured
# 2026-09-29. Negate the crate-level pins (not the root fixtures/ dir, which
# stays untracked at 1.7 GB).
!crates/*/fixtures/
!crates/*/fixtures/**
__pycache__/
scripts/aac-tables/sbr-cache.json
.cache/
lanes/wedge_dump
/graphify-out
